  "reason": "Cumulative Assistant-only port: exact Rust tests cover the durable journal, bounded fair queue, fixture CLI, 13 persisted record contracts, current-schema SQLite transactions, saved context/read cursors, paired-device authentication and bounded HTTP. The new navigation layer adds four storage tests for literal/scoped search, stored-row pagination, exact sequence ordering, complete reads past 1000 rows and 10k/16MiB bounds; four service tests for Unicode excerpts, durable inactive/reactivated bookmarks and timestamps, concurrent revision winners and queued session/message guards; one HTTP differential test compares 112 Python cases and 30 records after an actual database reopen. Existing nine HTTP tests cover shared validation/authentication/resource-limit regressions. Local navigation run: these 18 exact Rust tests and nine entity-store regressions for the shared one-row SQLite prefetch bound (27 total) plus the single Python navigation-oracle regeneration test. Cumulative CI: 66 exact Rust and 47 collected Python tests across the five explicitly listed feature/policy files. Rust collection/build limit 600 seconds per command, execution 120 seconds per exact test; Python local selected run 300 seconds; no full suites. Frozen Unicode 15 casefold mappings are generated with CPython3.12; existing Python-to-Rust-to-Python interoperability remains selected.",
  "exclusions": "No shipped listener or launch path changes. Seven experimental Assistant routes only. Remaining route/JSON syntax/content-type/method parity, CORS, diagnostics, streaming/reconnect, providers/harnesses, durable scheduling/recovery, historical/PostgreSQL/checkpoint migration, production desktop/mobile/LAN/device and performance gates remain incomplete. Figma inspection is design evidence only. New search retains legacy query costs and shared project lookup validates identity only. No live data/service, provider calls, real tools, other product areas, desktop-native changes or full suites.",
